course: dictionary
lesson: 8667
title: The word secrecy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Secrecy means keeping something secret, so that others do not find out. The ending -cy turns the word secret into a noun, a thing you can name. «Bletchley workers signed secrecy promises, and much of the story stayed secret until the 1970s.» Here secrecy means the promise to keep their work hidden.
explain: Secrecy is not always good. A surprise party or a plan made in secrecy in a story can be fun. But «it wants secrecy» is on the list of common signs of a scam. A trick that rushes you and asks you to hide things should make you stop and think.
explain: Some phrases help you use the word. «In secrecy» means done in a hidden way. «In great secrecy» means done with a lot of care to keep it hidden. «Sworn to secrecy» means someone has promised, firmly, not to tell.
fact: Secrecy is an uncountable noun, so you say great secrecy or some secrecy, not secrecies.
fact: Secrecy means keeping something secret so that others do not find out.
fact: «In secrecy» means done in a hidden way; «sworn to secrecy» means promised not to tell.
fact: «Bletchley workers signed secrecy promises»: their work stayed hidden until the 1970s.
fact: Some secrecy is unsafe: if an adult asks you to keep a secret that makes you feel unsafe, tell a trusted adult.
exercise: «Bletchley workers signed secrecy promises.» What does secrecy mean here? | Working very fast in a busy office | *Keeping their work hidden from others | Telling everyone about their work | Sending letters home to their families
exercise: A message says «Keep this secret, and do not tell your parents.» What should you do? | Tell a trusted adult | Send the password to the sender | Keep it, because secrets are always good | *Tell a trusted adult, because a secret that makes you feel unsafe is a warning
exercise: Find and copy the phrase that means done in a hidden way. | *in secrecy | secret until | story stayed | Bletchley workers
test: Which word means keeping something secret so that others do not find out? | Noise | Speed | *Secrecy | Shyness
test: Sam's friend says, «Promise you will never tell, not even your mum.» Is this always safe? | Yes, all secrets are fun and safe | Yes, because friends always know best | No, because secrets are never allowed | *No, a secret that makes you feel unsafe should be told to a trusted adult
exam: Which sentence uses secrecy correctly? | The team worked in secret secrecy on the surprise party. | The team worked in secrecy's on the surprise party. | The team worked in secrecies on the surprise party. | *The team worked in great secrecy on the surprise party.
